{"name":"Icelandic","hex":"#dae4ec","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Icelandic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A North Germanic language, the national tongue of Iceland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native or inhabitant of Iceland; an Icelander.","An Icelandic horse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Icelandic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Icelanders","blocks":[{"text":"Icelanders are an ethnic group and nation who are native to the island country of Iceland. They speak Icelandic, a North Germanic language."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Map_of_the_Icelandic_Diaspora_in_the_World.svg/330px-Map_of_the_Icelandic_Diaspora_in_the_World.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icelanders","wikidata":"Q191356"},{"title":"Icelandic language","blocks":[{"text":"Icelandic is a North Germanic language from the Indo-European language family spoken by about 390,000 people, the vast majority of whom live in Iceland, where it is the national language. Since it is a West Scandinavian language, it is most closely related to Faroese, western Norwegian dialects, and the extinct language Norn. It is not mutually intelligible with the continental Scandinavian languages and is more distinct from the most widely spoken Germanic languages, English and German. The written forms of Icelandic and Faroese are very similar, but their spoken forms are not mutually intelligible."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/%C3%8Dslendingas%C3%B6gur.jpg/330px-%C3%8Dslendingas%C3%B6gur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icelandic_language","wikidata":"Q294"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Rock_of_law_in_%C3%9Eingvellir.jpg/500px-Rock_of_law_in_%C3%9Eingvellir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Rock_of_law_in_%C3%9Eingvellir.jpg/500px-Rock_of_law_in_%C3%9Eingvellir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rock of law in Þingvellir was used to make speeches.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARock_of_law_in_%C3%9Eingvellir.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Lakagigar_Iceland_2004-07-01.jpg/500px-Lakagigar_Iceland_2004-07-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Lakagigar_Iceland_2004-07-01.jpg/500px-Lakagigar_Iceland_2004-07-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Laki erupted in 1783–84 with catastrophic consequences for Iceland.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALakagigar_Iceland_2004-07-01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/JonSigurdssonStatue.jpg/500px-JonSigurdssonStatue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/JonSigurdssonStatue.jpg/500px-JonSigurdssonStatue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Statue of Jón Sigurðsson in Reykjavík","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJonSigurdssonStatue.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Hvalsey_Church.jpg/500px-Hvalsey_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Hvalsey_Church.jpg/1280px-Hvalsey_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Hvalsey_Church.jpg/500px-Hvalsey_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p